    {
      "note": "Article on the toponym rectum, which the ASV renders anarthrously as *Gilead*, so its *the* is fronted (rule 29), exactly as at JOS.13.20 (*the slopes of Pisgah*) and JOS.13.33 (*the tribe of Levi*). An article MACULA segments off a toponym is never set aside as lexicalized in the name. The competing reading, taken in the earlier accepted alignment, supplied the *the* on the construct and marked this article unrepresented; that is the treatment for a phrase in which the ASV writes no *the* at all, as at JOS.13.11 and JOS.13.31, and it leaves a written *the* answering to no article while the article that licenses it holds nothing.",
